description:
When the browser has no valid nori_token cookie (fresh browser, expired session, etc.), navigating to any page causes an infinite redirect loop:

1. Navigate to / → hooks.server.ts calls /auth/me → 401 → redirect to /login
2. /login loads → root +layout.svelte mounts → authStore.initialize() → GET /auth/me → 401
3. ApiClient 401 handler does window.location.href = '/login' → full page reload
4. Go to step 2 → infinite loop

## Root Cause
Two issues working together:

### Issue A: ApiClient redirects to /login even when already on /login
File: web/src/lib/api/client.ts, lines 72-77 and 149-154
The 401 handler unconditionally does window.location.href = '/login' without checking if the user is already on an auth page.

### Issue B: authStore.initialize() runs on auth pages
File: web/src/routes/+layout.svelte, line 41
The root layout calls authStore.initialize() in onMount on every page, including /login. This triggers a GET /auth/me call that returns 401 (no cookie), which hits Issue A.

## Fix

### Fix A: client.ts — guard the 401 redirect
In both the request() method (line 72) and uploadFile() method (line 149), check window.location.pathname before redirecting:

```typescript
if (browser) {
  localStorage.removeItem('accessToken');
  localStorage.removeItem('activeSpaceId');
  const path = window.location.pathname;
  if (path !== '/login' && path !== '/change-password') {
    window.location.href = '/login';
  }
}
```

Apply this in BOTH places (request and uploadFile have duplicate 401 handling).

### Fix B: +layout.svelte — skip initialize on auth pages
The layout already computes isAuthPage. Use it in onMount:

```typescript
onMount(() => {
  if (!isAuthPage()) {
    authStore.initialize();
  }
  themeStore.initialize();
});
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Navigating to /login with no valid session does NOT cause infinite redirect/reload
- [ ] Navigating to a protected page with no valid session redirects to /login exactly once
- [ ] Logging in successfully still works (redirects to / or the redirectTo param)
- [ ] Logging out and being redirected to /login does not loop
- [ ] npm run check in web/ passes (pre-existing errors in spaces/[id] are acceptable)

Create shared TypeScript type definitions that match the backend Go DTOs, so all frontend code uses consistent types instead of inline interfaces.

## Files to Create
- `web/src/lib/types/task.ts` (new — the old one was deleted in US-001)
- `web/src/lib/types/station.ts`
- `web/src/lib/types/common.ts`

## Types to Define

### common.ts
- PaginatedResponse<T> — { items: T[], total: number, offset: number, limit: number }

### task.ts
- TaskStatus — 'open' | 'active' | 'paused' | 'done' | 'skipped' | 'cancelled'
- TaskType — 'job' | 'task' | 'milestone' | 'gate'
- TaskResponse — matches backend TaskResponse DTO (include ALL fields: id, spaceId, parentId, recipeId, recipeVersionId, stationId, customerId, assignedToId, createdById, type, status, title, description, priority, displayOrder, quantity, dueDate, startedAt, pausedAt, completedAt, actualTimeSeconds, deviationNotes, metadata, createdAt, updatedAt)
- TaskListResponse — PaginatedResponse<TaskResponse>
- TaskDep — { id: string, fromTaskId: string, toTaskId: string, type: string, createdAt: string }
- CreateTaskRequest — { title, description?, type, parentId?, stationId?, priority? }
- UpdateTaskRequest — { title?, description?, stationId?, priority?, status? }
- AddChildTaskRequest — { title, description?, type?, stationId?, afterId? }
- AddNoteRequest — { text }
- ReadyTask — matches what GET /tasks/ready returns (same as TaskResponse)

### station.ts
- StationResponse — { id, name, description, displayOrder, wipLimit, wipCount, bufferSize, isActive }
- CreateStationRequest — { name, description?, wipLimit?, bufferSize? }
- UpdateStationRequest — { name?, description?, wipLimit?, bufferSize?, isActive? }

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] All three type files exist with correct types matching backend DTOs
- [ ] TaskResponse includes the Quantity field (number, added in y2c.2)
- [ ] Types are exported and importable from their modules
- [ ] npm run check in web/ passes (pre-existing errors in spaces/[id] are acceptable)
